# The Philotes · the threads that connect all things

In Card's cosmology the philote is the smallest indivisible building block: a point with no parts, joined to others only by philotic rays, or twines. It is not matter in the ordinary sense but the connective substrate beneath matter — the place where things are tied to one another before they are anything else. From this single principle of connection the rest of the physics of the Enderverse unfolds.

Everything from atoms to stars to minds is bound in webs of philotic connection. The same threads that gather particles into bodies gather a body into a living unity, and gather a mind into a single bound self. Across the Ender Quintet, philotics is the quiet physics underneath the saga's larger events: faster-than-light ansible communication, the unity of a living body, and the bond of a mind to its own self all rest on this one foundation.

Its nature of emergence is ethereal because the philotic is, before all else, the connective and collective — the web rather than the things it holds. It is not a machine mind or a network of devices, nor a soul, nor an embodied creature, but the threads themselves: the unseen connection that lets separate points become one.
